    "notes": "Inspected all11 portable views. Sixteen individually mapped halls,27 roof ribbons, the paired courts, higher Birojeon/Gwaneumjeon/Nahanjeon terraces, two entrance stone bridges and three distinct pagodas form the specific Bulguksa exterior. Curved hip-and-gable roofs, red timber posts, muted green bracket bands and yellow wall fields are geometry. The main entrance has a real open barrel vault; the western entrance has lintel-and-pier supports. Dabotap retains four open pillars and four stairs, while Seokgatap has three solid decreasing storeys. The small sarira stupa is separately placed. The wider religious park and independent surrounding buildings are outside this model. Fine dancheong painting and sculpture are simplified. Portable fallback lighting is lighter than the textured Earth view; terrain and foundations were inspected separately in the actual-site renderer."
