    "notes": "Accepted for the specific medium-fi principal Bulguksa exterior and approximate full-site standard-map/DEM fit. Six ordinary references, including one visitor-style layout diagram, guide identity; pinned PMTiles roof/point controls determine horizontal placement. All16 actual roof controls and102 vertices remain intact. The main hall east axis is9.67 degrees north of east. Gallery ribbons are rectified within approximately55cm of their map envelope to suppress sub-metre jitter. Pagoda nominal heights10.4m/8.2m/2.1m follow ordinary reference descriptions, with approximate body/finial allocation. Heights, court thresholds, stair dimensions, curved roof sections, bays, brackets and stone profiles are visualization estimates. Twenty-seven floor pockets merge to ten meshes; six bounded openings affect only occupied ground. First-render foundation gaps were corrected with continuous retaining faces and inward entrance cut-bank joins, preserving the open vault. The original161-square/6m DEM is unchanged; only the portable source preview has occupied-floor seating. Partial loading clips the temple and bridge at temporary tile edges, so partial architectural completeness/contact remains pending. Exact carved details, inscriptions, deity figures, navigable interiors and the wider religious park are outside scope. No bespoke survey or archival research was used."
